WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:16.970
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon, is based on George RR

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.840
Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.710
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:31.529
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:34.149
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:40.690
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.240
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.110
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.859
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:58.739
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words, it covers events from Aegon's

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:03.289
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:08.530
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:14.490
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:19.280
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.460
One of the most popular Targaryens in history
and definitely the best warrior House Targaryen

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:29.550
ever produced is Aemon the Dragonknight, the
grandson of Rhaenyra Targaryen.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:33.720
The Dragonknight has been referred to as the
noblest and greatest knight that ever lived

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.050
and his skills with a sword were legendary
throughout Westeros.

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:41.820
Prince Aemon Targaryen, also known as the
Dragonknight, was a prince of the Targaryen

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.850
dynasty
and the second son of King Viserys II Targaryen

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:50.870
and grandson of Rhaenyra Targaryen who fought
in the Dance of the Dragons. Aemon joined

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:56.510
the Kingsguard during the reign of his uncle,
King Aegon III Targaryen, son of Rhaenyra,

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:02.500
at the age of seventeen, and eventually rose
to become Lord Commander. After Aegon III,

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.600
Aemon served four other kings.
He died saving the life of his brother, King

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.750
Aegon IV Targaryen.
Prince Aemon has been referred to as the noblest

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.370
knight who ever lived,
and his skill with a sword is legendary throughout

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:19.040
the Seven Kingdoms.
Even over a hundred years after his death,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:25.060
he is a popular figure among the highborn
and smallfolk in songs, stories, and fables.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.930
Aemon became known as the Dragonknight
because the crest on his helm was a three-headed

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.730
dragon of House Targaryen wrought in white
gold.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.480
As an infant, Aemon was large and strong,
and just as beautiful as his brother Aegon

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.981
was.
A dragon's egg was placed in his cradle. All

00:02:41.981 --> 00:02:45.440
rejoiced at his birth, except his older brother
Aegon,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.440
who was found by their mother hitting the
newborn Aemon with Aemon's egg.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.400
Aemon was inseparable from his sister Naerys
when they were young.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.250
Stories speak of Aemon's doomed love for his
sister. Aemon and Naerys supposedly loved

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:04.260
each other. According to the singers, both
Aemon and Naerys cried the day Naerys married

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:11.150
Aegon in 153 AC, although historians report
that Naerys had only cried during the bedding,

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.300
while Aemon had quarreled with Aegon at the
wedding feast.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.730
He became a great jouster and swordsman later
in life.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.349
The Dragonknight grew to be so accomplished
in the lists and with the sword that he was

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:27.139
deemed worthy of carrying the Valyrian steel
sword Dark Sister. Shortly after Naerys and

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:31.749
Aegon's wedding, Aemon joined the Kingsguard,
taking his vows at the age of seventeen during

00:03:31.749 --> 00:03:36.709
the reign of his uncle,
King Aegon III Targaryen known as the Dragonbane.

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:42.159
During his life, Aemon would serve under five
kings: his uncle Aegon III, his cousins Daeron

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:48.840
I and Baelor I, his father Viserys II, and
lastly his brother Aegon IV.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:55.309
Aemon once fought Lord Cregan Stark. Prince
Aemon claimed he never faced a finer swordsman.

00:03:55.309 --> 00:03:58.620
Cregan Stark, who fought for Rhaenyra during
the Targaryen civil war,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:03.030
considered Aemon to have been the best swordsman
he ever faced as well.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:07.239
The fight between the two happened shortly
before the Conquest of Dorne began.

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:11.430
The Dragonknight was around 20 and the Wolf
of Winterfell was around 50.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.870
Why did Cregan fight a grandson of a woman,
Rhaenyra Targaryen,

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.580
for whom he fought in the Dance of the Dragons,
you may ask.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:21.110
While the exact circumstances of this event
remain yet unknown,

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:26.139
I can tell you that Starks and Targaryens
were the closest of allies in this time period,

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:31.420
so Cregan and Aemon's fight was either a sparring
duel or they fought in a tourney.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.510
This would be the second time Cregan visited
Kings Landing,

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:38.220
the first time being in the Dance of the Dragons
when he ruled Kings Landing

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.440
in the event that came to be known as the
Hour of the Wolf.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.910
He came to Kings Landing bringing his son
and heir Rickon

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:49.360
as well as the northern army with him to join
King Daeron the Young Dragon in his Conquest

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.330
of Dorne.
Cregan’s son and heir Rickon accompanied

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.600
Aemon (in Daeron I’s army) for the Conquest
of Dorne.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.230
Rickon Stark fought bravely and died in this
conquest.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:04.790
During the invasion of Dorne, Aemon prevented
an assassination attempt on the Young Dragon

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:08.980
by throwing himself in the path of a poisoned
arrow meant for his king.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:13.470
Aemon survived the poison and was sent back
to King's Landing to recover.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.180
Upon his recovery Aemon returned to Dorne
to protect his king

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:22.610
and won great fame by defeating a Dornish
champion. A rebellion in Dorne undid Daeron's

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:27.630
conquest, however. Aemon was with Daeron when
he met the Dornishmen under a peace banner

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:33.850
in 161 AC, together with four other knights
of the Kingsguard. However, in betrayal, the

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:39.040
Dornishmen attacked Daeron and his knights.
The Young Dragon died with Blackfyre in his

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.970
hand, surrounded by a dozen enemies. Three
of those Kingsguard knights died defending

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:48.460
Daeron, one shamefully yielded,
and Aemon the Dragonknight was captured after

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:53.240
slaying two of the betrayers.
Lord Wyl of Wyl eventually put Aemon naked

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.460
in a crow cage placed above a pit filled with
vipers.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.960
The new king, Baelor I Targaryen, made peace
with the Prince of Dorne.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.170
On his return trip from Sunspear, Baelor tried
to free his cousin Aemon.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.040
House Wyl was told to release Aemon into Baelor's
custody,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.710
but instead, they gave Baelor the key of the
cage and an invitation to use it.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:18.150
The Dragonknight, fearing for his cousin and
new king's safety, begged Baelor to leave

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.340
him,
but Baelor refused and walked into the pit.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:26.180
Singers say the snakes bowed their heads
and refused to bite Baelor due to protection

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:31.590
from the gods. However, some maesters believe
Baelor was bitten six times before reaching

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.300
Aemon's cage, while Dornishmen claim the king
was bitten half a hundred times before using

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:40.140
the key. The freed Aemon carried Baelor upon
his back,

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.020
while the Wyls wagered on how long they would
last.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:48.520
The venom put Baelor in a coma, so Aemon carried
the comatose king north.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.370
The cousins arrived at Blackhaven, where the
castle's maester treated Baelor.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:56.670
The king eventually awoke upon the journey
to Storm's End,

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:01.170
but it was half a year more before he was
fit to travel to King's Landing.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:07.480
Aemon served during the brief reign of his
father Viserys II Targaryen, king from 171

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:12.490
AC to 172 AC.
Aemon's elder brother, Aegon IV, succeeded

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:16.890
their father, Viserys II.
During Aegon's reign, Aemon remained the Lord

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:21.590
Commander of the Kingsguard,
a position he held until his death. When Naerys

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:26.480
was accused of adultery and treason by Ser
Morgil, Prince Aemon defended his sister's

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:32.920
honor in trial by combat and slew Morgil.
This inspired many songs and furthered Aemon's

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:38.110
renown, much to King Aegon's annoyance.
Rumors remained about Aemon being the actual

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:43.450
father of Aegon's son and heir, Prince Daeron.
This caused several people to look at one

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:48.430
of Aegon's bastards, Daemon Blackfyre,
as the new heir to the throne. The truth of

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:54.130
these rumors have never been proven or disproven.
Disguised as a mystery knight, Prince Aemon

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:58.800
once won a tourney after his brother Aegon
had forbidden him to take part, because Aegon

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.450
wanted to crown his mistress of that time
as the queen of love and beauty. Disguised

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:08.620
as the Knight of Tears, Aemon won the tournament
and named Naerys Targaryen in place of the

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:14.750
mistress. Despite Aegon's feelings of disrespect
and hatred towards Aemon and Aegon's provocations,

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:19.990
Aemon died honorably, defending his brother
and king against the assassination attempt

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:24.370
by two brothers of House Toyne
who sought revenge for the torture and execution

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:29.100
of their brother, Ser Terrence Toyne.
Queen Naerys grieved Aemon's death and died

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:34.769
in childbirth a year later.
King Aegon IV did little to honor the Dragonknight's

00:08:34.769 --> 00:08:38.180
memory.
Aegon began to make barely-veiled references

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:43.210
to his son Daeron's alleged illegitimacy,
something he only dared to do because both

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:47.230
Naerys and Aemon were dead.
Aegon's attempts to blacken his brother's

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:51.110
name failed,
as Aemon is remembered as a heroic figure

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:55.780
on par with legends of the Age of Heroes
and his memory greatly respected throughout

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.280
Westeros,
while the king was posthumously dubbed Aegon

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.231
the Unworthy.
Daeron II, Aemon's nephew (or son, according

00:09:03.231 --> 00:09:06.680
to rumors),
named his grandson Maester Aemon Targaryen

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:10.230
in honor of the Dragonknight.
Aemon the Dragonknight will definitely be

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:14.580
one of my favorite characters in the House
of the Dragon, although his time will come

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:18.550
in the later seasons of the show.
An honorable man who not only upholds his

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:24.320
oath to his brother and King Aegon the Unworthy
even upon the worst of insults, but also dies

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.970
to save his life.
The noblest knight that ever lived and the

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:32.030
best warrior of his time,
and likely the best warrior in the history

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:35.930
of Westeros.
Legendary characters such as Aemon the Dragonknight

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:40.870
and a dozen more legendary characters coming
before and after him, legendary battles such

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:45.220
as the Conquest of Dorne
and many more coming before and after as well,

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:49.020
all of that and more this Game of Thrones
prequel show, House of the Dragon, brings

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:53.050
in 2022 on HBO.
Let me know your thoughts about all of this

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.529
in the comment section down below.
Thank you so much for watching and I hope

00:09:55.529 --> 00:10:02.050
to see you in the next one.
Peace!

